| §C9.a NOVELTY_CHALLENGES — Divisor-only restriction at primorial Q: does `M_W^{div}(n) := Σ_{q | W, q sqf} mu(gcd(q,n)) / phi(q/gcd(q,n))` admit an exact pointwise closed form? (cross-domain: NONE; project-internal Möbius collapse + Hölder-reduced Ramanujan sum) | BUILT | E | S208 novelty-mode session refining E2.1 / S191 / C9. **Theorem (S208, proven analytically; verified pointwise to machine epsilon at N ≤ 10⁶ across 10 conductors).** For every squarefree integer W ≥ 1 and every positive integer n, `M_W^{div}(n) = [gcd(n, W) = 1] · W / phi(W)`. For non-squarefree W, the identity holds with W replaced by rad(W). **Proof**: factorise the squarefree-divisor lattice of W by intersection with `{p|W : p|n}`; the alternating-sum collapse `Σ_{A⊆P_n}(-1)^|A| = [P_n = ∅]` factors out, leaving `∏_{p|W} p/(p-1) = W/φ(W)` on the coprime branch. **Empirical verification**: 10 conductors `W ∈ {2, 6, 30, 210, 2310 (primorials); 15, 105 (squarefree non-primorial); 12, 60, 420 (non-squarefree, rad ∈ {6, 30, 210})}` × `N ∈ {10⁵, 10⁶}`. F1/F2/F3 (pointwise identity at squarefree primorial / squarefree non-primorial / radical-reduced non-squarefree): max abs_err 8.88·10⁻¹⁶ (machine epsilon). F4 (mean = 1): all in [0.999997, 1.000000]. F5 (L² closed form `||T_W^{div} − chi_P||²/N` matches explicit prime-distribution count `(n_coprime_primes (T_val−1)² + n_coprime_comp T_val² + n_W) / N` with `T_val = (π(N)/N) · W/φ(W)`): rel_err < 10⁻⁹ on every cell. F6 (Pearson_full > Pearson_div for W ∈ {6, 30, 210, 2310}): PASS, gap = 0.028, 0.089, 0.177, 0.281 respectively at N=10⁵; gap = 0 at W=2 because the only squarefree integers ≤ 2 are exactly the divisors of 2. **Algorithmic consequence**: T_W^{div}(n) is informationally equivalent to a wheel-rad(W) sieve scaled by π(N)/N · rad(W)/φ(rad(W)); the divisor-only restriction inherits all sieve barriers (no polylog opening). The Pearson gap to full T_W locates the prime-discriminating signal in the **non-divisor squarefree conductors** q ≤ W (q